2FA reliability audit - 2026-08-11 CST

ROOT CAUSES OBSERVED
- Re-authentication could reuse the registration OTP; the server returned HTTP 401.
- Older activation endpoints rejected or required factor_type inconsistently (HTTP 422).
- TOTP codes generated close to a 30-second boundary could expire before activation (HTTP 403 invalid_code).
- Enrollment/activation had transient HTTP 500/5xx responses.
- Browser fetches could outlive the Selenium async-script timeout, surfacing as an unclassified driver timeout.

FIXED BEHAVIORS
- Fresh-window TOTP generation with a minimum remaining lifetime and next-window retry.
- Bounded retries for enrollment/activation on invalid-code and transient 429/5xx responses.
- factor_type compatibility fallback for old and new endpoint variants.
- Browser fetch AbortController timeout plus a Selenium script timeout larger than the fetch window.
- Driver timeout exceptions normalized into the 2FA stage error; activation checks session MFA state before retrying an ambiguous timeout.
- Browser requests include origin/referer and stage names for actionable logs.

